  message: "DONE in PR #1341 (merged, dev 629cff5c1f).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the filed repro re-run on merged dev (String k = System.getenv(\"API_KEY\"); System.out.println(k);):\n  survey edge: calls java:java.io.PrintStream:0-0:println (call_construct method, io_target_kind std_stream) -- was java:external:0-0:println\n  host_secret -> ipc:      CONFIRMED, no caveat -- was confirmed_with_caveats, unknown_receiver_scope entries [println] (1 of 1 sites)\n  host_secret -> logging:  VIOLATED, ONE row [java.io.PrintStream.println] (the System.out attribute folds into its carrier, INV-hopib)\n  control, a PrintStream PARAMETER (ps.println(k)): unchanged -- inconclusive on both claims, disclosed as external_potential java.io.PrintStream.println\nA local named `out` no longer lends System.out its type (test_java_stdio_receiver_typed).\n\nTHE ITEM'S FIX SHAPE WAS INCOMPLETE, as recorded on 09-30: typing alone trades the caveat for inconclusive (java grants no module_completeness). Shipped instead, owner-authorized JDK surface in hand (JDK 25.0.2 reflected via jdk4py + JPype1 from PyPI after the docker socket was refused; docs/surveys/java-printstream-io-enumeration.md):\n- a new catalogue row key, requires_target_kind: the row applies only where every site's stamp resolves to it, and an unstamped call is NOT classified (no abstention). Validated at load; io_boundary narrows it; taint marks the sink gated with no fallback.\n- java.yaml: java.io.PrintStream's writing surface (append format print printf println write writeBytes flush checkError) as logging, requires_target_kind std_stream. NO completeness grant (the corpus census found PrintStreams over buffers, files and sockets, 308 as parameters -- no safe default).\nA/B pre-registered (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dorus_09302026/RESULT.md, 7 java repos x 7 claims): no verdict moved; 16 unknown_receiver_scope entries gone (println/printf/print only); logging +315 chains, all PrintStream writers; every removed System.out/err atom has its PrintStream twin. One refutation: cassandra's System.out.close() is now DISCLOSED as an external_potential gap where the `external` placeholder used to hide it -- the intended \"stays unclassified\", made visible.\nThe 09-26 census numbers (cassandra 383, jenkins 125, sherpa-onnx 186 untyped sites) were not re-counted as such; the per-claim caveat entries above are what was measured.\nNOT covered: kotlin / scala files (their analyzers emit neither the attribute ref nor this typing) -- WI-rabum."  # 984e
